# The assistant behind /api/chat. Any OpenAI-compatible host of open models works;
# copy this to .env.local and fill in the key.
#
# Groq (the default), Together, OpenRouter, DeepInfra, Fireworks, local Ollama.
CHAT_API_KEY=
# CHAT_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# CHAT_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.8-27b
# Thinking off — the answers are recall, not reasoning, and it halves the bill.
# Values are per-model (qwen3 takes "none"); empty omits the parameter.
# CHAT_REASONING_EFFORT=none

# The Inbox's send button (/api/contact). https://resend.com/api-keys
# CONTACT_EMAIL is where messages land and is never sent to the browser — keep it
# out of data/tree.ts, which ships in the page source.
RESEND_API_KEY=
CONTACT_EMAIL=you@example.com
# CONTACT_FROM=Portfolio <hello@yourdomain.com>

# --- Durable rate limiting (optional) -----------------------------------------
# Without these, /api/contact still rate limits, but only within one edge isolate
# — a speed bump, not a guarantee. Set both and the counter moves to Redis, which
# is what makes the limit hold across regions and restarts.
# Free tier at https://upstash.com — create a Redis DB, copy the REST creds.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
